{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0a74b819a7480753aa876342746598bdfe2258d89b2a31763bae36761d981001"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Makefile exposes operational commands such as make start, monitor, status, health, history, export, stop, pause, and resume, plus a Next.js dashboard runnable on port 3000."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1798dfaec9bdee2883e3cd53b17f79eda74d5d6fc76f12dd61ff9effdf1f3568"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Consensus.md acts as the relay baton carrying state between cycles, written atomically via a .consensus.tmp temp file and rename, with a .bak backup restored automatically on cycle failure."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8bac5388a7862c739ce4f150b191cfc5d1c1a50cfc84e7ea8a45ba7fb7a3b3a3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration is environment-based via .env, with documented variables including MODEL (default sonnet), LOOP_INTERVAL (120s), CYCLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (1800s), MAX_CONSECUTIVE_ERRORS (3), and COOLDOWN_SECONDS (300)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c9fe278c0bbdac0610debda0408f1dc1b15947791c49d293626a6b4be2007ad5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The loop includes resilience mechanisms: a circuit breaker after MAX_CONSECUTIVE_ERRORS failures with a cooldown, and automatic sleep of LIMIT_WAIT_SECONDS (default one hour) on API usage-limit errors."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0a74b819a7480753aa876342746598bdfe2258d89b2a31763bae36761d981001","clm_1798dfaec9bdee2883e3cd53b17f79eda74d5d6fc76f12dd61ff9effdf1f3568","clm_8bac5388a7862c739ce4f150b191cfc5d1c1a50cfc84e7ea8a45ba7fb7a3b3a3","clm_c9fe278c0bbdac0610debda0408f1dc1b15947791c49d293626a6b4be2007ad5"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:12:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_b4c60094b5cd4e1c921e4ce136242946","id":"pg_1d59985cf9445ced9afda86e58cf402a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/nikitadmitrieff-auto-co-meta-docs-devops-runbook-md-5e6bb8a8765e-a86e58cf402a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_19e7da2